# ── Generated registers (MOD-548) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Written by the generators of the docs/tools/regen.py roster; since MOD-548 they are regenerated
# once per push (.githooks/pre-push), not on every commit. In the 30 days before that change
# docs/tasks/README.md was rewritten 564 times and COVERAGE.md 295, and review — plus `git log -p`
# — drowned in those regenerations.
#
#   linguist-generated=true — GitHub collapses the file in a pull-request diff and leaves it out of
#                             the language statistics;
#   -diff                   — git builds no line diff locally (`git diff` says "Binary files …
#                             differ"). To look inside once: `git diff --text` / `git log -p --text`.
#
#   merge=regenerated       — (MOD-718) a conflict keeps our side without asking: pre-push
#                             regenerates the file anyway (ADR-019). The driver is `true`, set by
#                             `./gradlew installGitHooks`; without it git merges textually, as before.
#                             Only pure functions of the tree carry it: COVERAGE.md holds a CI snapshot
#                             of L1 read back by its own generator, so it keeps a loud conflict, and so
#                             do docs/tasks/.next_id (an ID collision must be seen) and the MOD-699
#                             registry snapshot (a reference updated only by an explicit command).
#
# The text/eol attributes are DELIBERATELY left alone here: docs/tools/repo/line_endings_check.py
# reads them as the single oracle for "which line ending is prescribed", and `-diff` does not touch
# that answer.
#
# Deliberately NOT listed: files where the generated part is one region inside a hand-written page —
# docs/ROADMAP.md (`AUTO:released`, `AUTO:advancement-count`), docs/testing/progression/advancements.md
# and docs/blocks/*/index.md (`AUTO:planned`). There the diff is what you want: the hand-written text
# is the content and the generated region is an inset. In docs/tasks/README.md and
# docs/roadmap/README.md the `AUTO:` region is most of the file, which is why they are listed.
docs/tasks/README.md              linguist-generated=true -diff merge=regenerated
docs/tasks/archive/README.md      linguist-generated=true -diff merge=regenerated
docs/roadmap/README.md            linguist-generated=true -diff merge=regenerated
docs/testing/TRACEABILITY.md      linguist-generated=true -diff merge=regenerated
docs/testing/COVERAGE.md          linguist-generated=true -diff
tools/crafts_board.html           linguist-generated=true -diff merge=regenerated
tools/recipes_graph.html          linguist-generated=true -diff merge=regenerated
tools/showcase.html               linguist-generated=true -diff merge=regenerated
tools/advancement_tree.html       linguist-generated=true -diff merge=regenerated
docs/tools/block_graph.html       linguist-generated=true -diff merge=regenerated
